{
  "requirement": "GitHub Actions MUST run `cargo test --locked --workspace` and `mdbook test` for pull requests and pushes to `main`. After those checks pass on `main`, it MUST build the book and deploy the generated `book/` directory to GitHub Pages. The book MUST set `output.html.site-url` to `/habeas-codicem/` for project-site hosting.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The behavior is mostly present, but nothing in the project is marked as implementing or testing `requirements.integration.ci`.\n\n**What is implemented**\n- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` triggers on `push` to `main` and on `pull_request`.\n- The `test-and-build` job runs `cargo test --locked --workspace` and `mdbook test`, then `mdbook build`. It uploads the `book` directory as the Pages artifact on pushes.\n- The `deploy` job is limited to pushes on `refs/heads/main` and uses `actions/deploy-pages@v4`. It depends on `needs: [test-and-build, symposium-hook]`.\n- `book.toml` sets `site-url = \"/habeas-codicem/\"` under `[output.html]`.\n\n**Gaps**\n1. **No `{impl}` marking.** The `references` lookup for `requirements.integration.ci` returns no sites. Neither `ci.yml` nor `book.toml` carries a `{impl}` marker for it. Other integration requirements, such as `symposium` and `symposium_cli` in `Cargo.toml`, are marked this way. The workflow and the `site-url` setting are code that implements the requirement without an `{impl}` reference, which counts as a gap.\n2. **No `{test}` reference.** No test or other verification is tied to this requirement. A test such as a unit check that parses `ci.yml` and `book.toml` would be practical, and the project already tests its other workflow behavior with scripts. No FIXME acknowledges the absence.\n3. **Behavior the requirement does not specify.** The CI workflow also runs the autofix controller tests (`node --test`) and a separate `symposium-hook` job. Deployment depends on both, and neither is mentioned in this requirement. The requirement only names the two checks that must pass before deploy.\n\nBecause the gaps are unmarked and not acknowledged by a FIXME, the determination is false.",
